From 80f4f6fea5f9e60ccd835c7c5fac9491c5fabe04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 07:55:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: use SDL_Delay for frame pacing, not Thread::staticSleep

Root cause of the whole real-hardware silent-audio investigation:
Passage's frame-rate limiter called minorGems' Thread::staticSleep(),
which on DOS (ThreadDOS.cpp) is a raw usleep() that bypasses SDL
entirely. This shared DOS backend's audio playback runs on a
cooperative-scheduler mechanism that only gets handed CPU time via
SDL_Delay() specifically (see SDL_dosaudio_sb.c's DOS_Yield
commentary -- the per-flip SDL_Delay(0) is the documented hook that
lets the audio thread run at all).

Since Passage never called SDL_Delay() anywhere, that cooperative
audio pump never ran: the device opened successfully (that happens
synchronously, before the main loop), but PlayDevice/WaitDevice never
executed even once. Confirmed directly: SDL_HINT_DOS_SILENCE_HISTO=1
(an existing shared-backend diagnostic) showed zero emits at all
before this fix -- not "all silent," literally no PlayDevice calls --
and after this fix, real emits appear with a genuine noisy_n>0 (real,
non-silent mixed content reaching PlayDevice), confirmed under
DOSBox-X. This explains every symptom observed across this entire
investigation (the original live-synthesis audio, and Phase A's
pre-rendered-buffer replacement, were both equally silent) since
neither implementation could ever be the cause -- the callback was
never being pumped at all, regardless of what it computed.

Single call site (game.cpp's per-frame extraTime sleep); no other
Thread::staticSleep call sites exist in gameSource/.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index b92f82f..a077fc5 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -1002,7 +1002,15 @@ char playGame() {
         double extraTime = 1.0 / lockedFrameRate - frameTime;
         
         if( extraTime > 0 ) {
-            Thread::staticSleep( (int)( extraTime * 1000 ) );
+            // DOS-PORT: SDL_Delay, not Thread::staticSleep -- on DOS,
+            // Thread::staticSleep is a raw usleep() that bypasses SDL
+            // entirely (see ThreadDOS.cpp). This backend's cooperative
+            // audio-thread scheduler only gets CPU time via SDL_Delay
+            // (its DOS_Yield hook); without this, the audio device opens
+            // fine but PlayDevice/WaitDevice never run at all, and
+            // nothing pushed into the ring is ever mixed or played,
+            // regardless of what the audio callback computes.
+            SDL_Delay( (Uint32)( extraTime * 1000 ) );
             }
 
         // start timing next frame
-- 
2.47.3

